# The repo checks out CRLF on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) while the index
# holds LF: `git ls-files --eol` reported 315 of 320 text files as i/lf w/crlf.
# That split silently breaks scripted edits — a codemod matching a multi-line
# anchor with \n matches nothing, changes no files, and reports success.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the working tree agree with the index. The index is
# already LF, so this commit changes no file content; it only stops the next
# developer's autocrlf setting from deciding the answer.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.jsx  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
